  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer array `nums`, output *the number of triplets chosen from the array that can make triangles if we take them as side lengths of a triangle*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [2,2,3,4]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: Valid combinations are: \n2,3,4 (using the first 2)\n2,3,4 (using the second 2)\n2,2,3\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [4,2,3,4]\nOutput: 4\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n* `0 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
